WEBVTT

00:02.580 --> 00:06.340
Good morning, Haruto...

00:10.430 --> 00:12.050
Morning.

00:16.060 --> 00:19.080
<i>My classes are finally about to begin.</i>

00:19.080 --> 00:20.390
Haruto.

00:21.250 --> 00:23.980
Let me explain your schedule for today.

00:23.980 --> 00:25.470
Ah, sure.

00:27.830 --> 00:30.900
I believe that with exemptions 
based on the entrance exam,

00:30.900 --> 00:34.100
you'll be placed into the 
very middle class, C Class.

00:34.100 --> 00:35.340
I see.

00:35.590 --> 00:39.570
That said, classes are shuffled 
based on regular exam performance,

00:39.570 --> 00:43.390
so I'm sure that you'll be able 
to move up to A Class in no time!

00:43.390 --> 00:45.560
<i>Man, I hope not.</i>

00:45.810 --> 00:49.100
Wait, other than the core curriculum,

00:49.100 --> 00:52.140
these are all really hard 
upper-grade classes!

00:52.550 --> 00:55.750
I picked them because I 
knew you'd find them easy.

00:55.750 --> 00:57.630
<i>Nope, not happening!</i>

00:58.090 --> 01:01.430
<i>Or maybe that could work to my advantage.</i>

01:01.970 --> 01:04.750
<i>If I choose all of these advanced classes,</i>

01:02.450 --> 01:06.670
Hm? How cocky for
a first-year...

01:04.460 --> 01:07.710
Let's see how you do

01:04.750 --> 01:07.630
<i>the teachers will end up having 
extremely high expectations of me.</i>

01:06.460 --> 01:10.590
So much for that

01:07.500 --> 01:10.590
He's nothing special!

01:07.630 --> 01:10.410
<i>Giving me the perfect 
chance to let them down!</i>

01:09.460 --> 01:10.590
How disappointing

01:10.860 --> 01:12.950
<i>Okay! Sounds good!</i>

01:12.950 --> 01:14.330
Haruto.

01:14.330 --> 01:15.000
Hmm?

01:24.560 --> 01:26.390
Have a good day at school!

01:26.920 --> 01:28.990
Yeah. I'll try.

01:31.690 --> 01:32.740
Long hug, don't you think?

01:33.340 --> 01:36.540
Parting is always such a shame.

01:37.770 --> 01:40.600
Squeeze...

01:38.090 --> 01:40.370
I see...

01:59.470 --> 02:02.850
<b>Am I Actually the Strongest?</b>

03:11.500 --> 03:17.050
m 0 0 l 50 0 l 45 13 l -5 13

03:11.500 --> 03:17.050
Episode 11

03:11.500 --> 03:17.050
<b>I Got Myself Mixed Up with so Many People...</b>

03:13.860 --> 03:15.450
Good morning, Haruto!

03:15.450 --> 03:16.790
Good morning.

03:17.270 --> 03:18.770
And who's this?

03:18.770 --> 03:20.300
My attendant, Liza.

03:23.740 --> 03:26.510
I wouldn't put it past Haruto's attendant...

03:27.350 --> 03:29.830
I'm Iris, Haruto's friend.

03:29.830 --> 03:30.650
It's a pleasure.

03:31.160 --> 03:32.850
Nice to meet you.

03:36.380 --> 03:37.260
What?

03:37.490 --> 03:40.420
You're in C Class, with your skills?

03:40.420 --> 03:42.230
I'm in A Class.

03:42.540 --> 03:45.820
I was told that written exam 
grades are given priority,

03:45.820 --> 03:49.330
so I'm sure you'll join 
me in A Class very soon.

03:49.330 --> 03:50.900
Ah, yeah.

03:52.070 --> 03:53.790
Excuse me, Lord Haruto.

03:53.790 --> 03:56.180
Is she really human?

03:57.170 --> 03:59.350
Even observing her up close,

03:59.350 --> 04:03.260
I can't tell whether she's 
a demon or a human.

04:03.590 --> 04:06.890
From what I can tell, she's not a demon.

04:06.890 --> 04:09.750
She doesn't seem evil, so we 
shouldn't worry about it.

04:10.520 --> 04:11.970
Okay.

04:22.810 --> 04:25.360
<i>Why's everyone staring at me?</i>

04:25.700 --> 04:30.230
<i>Oh, I forgot I was the talk of 
the school, thanks to Schneidel.</i>

04:30.780 --> 04:32.710
Let's begin our class.

04:32.930 --> 04:36.400
This is C Class, the middle 
class of the five we offer,

04:36.400 --> 04:39.620
with grades in the median range overall.

04:39.620 --> 04:42.720
In other words, you have a chance 
of climbing your way up,

04:42.720 --> 04:44.650
as well as dropping down instead.

04:44.650 --> 04:46.060
Which is why...

04:46.390 --> 04:49.150
you will be taking another test today.

04:49.440 --> 04:51.120
<i>It's here already!</i>

04:51.120 --> 04:52.670
<i>My big chance!</i>

04:52.670 --> 04:55.830
<i>I'll use this exam to show 
them how incompetent I am</i>

04:55.830 --> 04:58.430
<i>and say goodbye to this 
classroom on day one!</i>

04:58.830 --> 05:00.680
Now then, begin.

05:02.060 --> 05:02.840
Huh?

05:03.620 --> 05:06.310
<i>This is a walk in the park!</i>

05:06.700 --> 05:09.960
<i>I think when Char was young and 
began her gifted education,</i>

05:09.960 --> 05:12.360
<i>she covered this material 
in the first six months.</i>

05:12.630 --> 05:15.490
<i>Putting questions on here that 
even infants can solve...</i>

05:15.490 --> 05:17.560
<i>What is this teacher up to?</i>

05:21.450 --> 05:23.670
<i>Oh, I see what he's doing!</i>

05:23.980 --> 05:25.580
<i>After threatening everyone like that,</i>

05:25.580 --> 05:29.510
<i>he's trying to reassure everyone with basic 
problems that are actually really easy.</i>

05:29.860 --> 05:33.310
<i>Which makes it difficult 
to know how to respond.</i>

05:33.780 --> 05:36.790
<i>If I get so many simple questions wrong,</i>

05:36.790 --> 05:39.660
<i>they might suspect I'm 
doing it intentionally.</i>

05:40.330 --> 05:41.360
<i>In that case,</i>

05:41.610 --> 05:43.760
<i>I'll find the absolute minimum borderline,</i>

05:43.760 --> 05:46.320
<i>and aim to get a 60 with careless mistakes!</i>

05:46.780 --> 05:48.990
<b>Testing Over</b>

05:50.420 --> 05:54.210
It looks like the results are quite poor.

05:54.550 --> 05:57.530
The average ended up barely scratching a 20.

05:57.790 --> 05:58.890
<i>Hmm?</i>

05:58.890 --> 06:00.760
Well, I'm not surprised.

06:01.010 --> 06:05.460
Even B Class students would average 
around a 50 on this material.

06:05.770 --> 06:07.690
Ah, I knew it!

06:07.690 --> 06:09.100
<i>Huh? What the heck?</i>

06:09.410 --> 06:12.670
Despite this, and even with 
plenty of careless mistakes,

06:12.670 --> 06:15.280
one of you managed to get around a 60.

06:15.280 --> 06:18.920
Haruto Zenfis! Bravo!

06:22.400 --> 06:24.200
<i>What's going on?!</i>

06:24.200 --> 06:26.240
<i>Was I the only one who got easy problems?!</i>

06:26.240 --> 06:28.190
<i>No, that's not it.</i>

06:28.190 --> 06:30.980
<i>It's not that they're all 
at a low academic level.</i>

06:30.980 --> 06:33.990
<i>That said, it's not like I'm 
particularly advanced, either.</i>

06:33.990 --> 06:35.020
Sparkle!

06:35.020 --> 06:38.190
<i>My little sister is just too outstanding!</i>

06:38.480 --> 06:40.530
Haruto Zenfis!

06:40.530 --> 06:45.250
I'll put in a good word, so you move 
up to A Class before the next lesson!

06:45.570 --> 06:47.830
<i>Gloom...</i>

06:56.370 --> 06:57.090
Eh?

07:02.440 --> 07:03.770
Hey, lady.

07:03.770 --> 07:05.040
Stop clinging to Haruto.

07:05.040 --> 07:07.000
You're the one who's too close to Haruto.

07:07.000 --> 07:08.290
What was that?!

07:08.290 --> 07:09.290
Huh?!

07:10.830 --> 07:13.660
<i>Sheesh, why's this happening to me?</i>

07:16.530 --> 07:17.990
It's time.

07:17.990 --> 07:19.420
I assume you're all here.

07:19.830 --> 07:22.630
I am your professor, Oratoria Belkam.

07:22.630 --> 07:25.130
I'm an expert in elemental theory.

07:25.400 --> 07:28.600
<i>Ugh, she seems like a hardass.</i>

07:30.380 --> 07:32.220
You three first-years!

07:32.220 --> 07:36.320
You're only in your first year, 
yet you signed up for my advanced class.

07:36.320 --> 07:41.300
You've got some nerve, sitting in the 
very front and chatting right away.

07:41.300 --> 07:46.050
I'll kick all of you out the moment that 
you can't answer one of my questions.

07:46.050 --> 07:47.780
Prepare yourselves.

07:48.060 --> 07:51.200
Not to mention, 
Haruto Zenfis and Irisphilia...

07:51.200 --> 07:55.500
I hear you two joined that 
four-eyed runt's research lab.

07:55.870 --> 07:57.310
Ah, yes.

07:57.310 --> 07:58.360
What of it?

07:59.500 --> 08:03.240
I'll make sure to be extra 
diligent in teaching you two!

08:03.240 --> 08:03.920
<i>What?!</i>

08:03.920 --> 08:05.330
<i>Did we catch a stray bullet?!</i>

08:07.480 --> 08:12.800
Today's lesson is on main elements, 
sub-elements, and quantification.

08:13.200 --> 08:14.650
Irisphilia.

08:14.650 --> 08:16.620
Come here and put your hands on this.

08:21.620 --> 08:22.560
Oh?

08:22.810 --> 08:24.800
You possess every element?

08:24.800 --> 08:26.520
What a magnificent sight.

08:26.790 --> 08:30.610
It truly is a shame that 
your mana level is at a five!

08:30.610 --> 08:32.610
Join my research lab!

08:32.610 --> 08:34.960
I'll thoroughly whip you into shape!

08:35.570 --> 08:37.700
No, I'm afraid I must decline.

08:37.700 --> 08:39.970
Tsk. How disappointing.

08:42.450 --> 08:46.640
The element that one is most proficient 
at is known as their main element.

08:46.640 --> 08:49.600
For Irisphilia, that would be chaos.

08:49.600 --> 08:53.300
Displayed below are all of her sub-elements.

08:53.590 --> 08:57.010
And well, that's all that 
a crystal can tell us.

08:57.470 --> 08:59.580
If we take the main element to be 100%,

08:59.580 --> 09:02.380
how well can someone 
control the sub-elements?

09:02.380 --> 09:07.240
There's research being done to quantify 
it, but it's proven difficult.

09:07.240 --> 09:10.040
<i>Is it really that difficult?</i>

09:11.280 --> 09:14.150
<i>Mana Calculator: Revised, activate!</i>

09:14.150 --> 09:19.370
Irisphilia
[05] / [35]
Main Element [Chaos] 100 - [Disorder]
 Sub-Elements [Darkness] 91 - [Abyss]
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h[High Power]
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h[Status Recovery]
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h[Water] 87 -\h\h\h\h[Status Recovery]
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h[Wind] 84 - \h\h\h\h\h[Flight]
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h[Fire] 87 -\h\h\h\h\h\h\h[High Power]
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h[Earth] 78 -\h\h\h\h\h[Sturdy]
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h[Light] 17 - \h\h\h\h[Reduced Purification]
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h[Reduced Power]
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h[Reduced Range]

09:15.160 --> 09:19.360
<i>Looks like the one I made 
displays it just fine.</i>

09:19.670 --> 09:22.810
So why is quantification so difficult?

09:23.770 --> 09:26.670
It's because circumstances 
can alter the values.

09:27.160 --> 09:30.670
Imagine that fire is your sub-element, 
and you use a muscle-enhancing spell.

09:31.110 --> 09:34.950
And you find that it has an increased 
rate compared to other fire spells.

09:35.240 --> 09:36.780
Why is that the case?

09:36.780 --> 09:39.170
Answer me, Laius Olteas.

09:41.690 --> 09:44.050
Does it have to do with the 
degree of proficiency?

09:44.050 --> 09:47.270
By using muscle enhancement over 
and over, you end up mastering it?

09:47.520 --> 09:49.940
Not a terrible way to approach the problem.

09:49.940 --> 09:53.490
However, research contradicts 
that conjecture of yours.

09:53.810 --> 09:56.400
Which means it's due to hidden properties.

09:59.210 --> 09:59.770
Whoa!

10:00.170 --> 10:02.020
Haruto Zenfis.

10:02.020 --> 10:04.320
What did you just say?

10:04.980 --> 10:07.280
<i>Ah, I messed up.</i>

10:07.290 --> 10:14.590
Irisphilia
[05] / [35]
Main Element [Chaos] 100 - [Disorder]
 Sub-Elements [Darkness] 91 - [Abyss]
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h[High Power]
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h[Status Recovery]
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h[Water] 87 -\h\h\h\h[Status Recovery]
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h[Wind] 84 - \h\h\h\h\h[Flight]
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h[Fire] 87 -\h\h\h\h\h\h\h[High Power]
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h[Earth] 78 -\h\h\h\h\h[Sturdy]
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h[Light] 17 - \h\h\h\h[Reduced Purification]
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h[Reduced Power]
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h[Reduced Range]

10:07.670 --> 10:11.710
<i>My Revised Mana Calculator 
also shows some odd terms.</i>

10:11.710 --> 10:15.110
<i>I've been calling them 
"hidden properties"...</i>

10:15.110 --> 10:20.140
<i>And I've only ever mentioned 
them to Char and the others...</i>

10:20.140 --> 10:21.840
Answer me!

10:21.850 --> 10:32.980
<b>[Fire] - Enhance</b>

10:22.480 --> 10:26.600
I think there are hidden properties 
that are subordinate to elements.

10:26.600 --> 10:30.310
For example, if the fire element had 
a hidden property of "Enhance,"

10:30.310 --> 10:33.420
it would increase the effects 
of self-enhancement spells.

10:34.740 --> 10:36.780
How do you know that?!

10:36.780 --> 10:39.100
That's cutting-edge research 
from Weiße Eule!

10:39.910 --> 10:42.070
Weiße Eule?

10:42.270 --> 10:43.690
A mysterious individual

10:43.690 --> 10:48.420
who irregularly sends us research 
papers, as of a few years ago.

10:48.820 --> 10:52.040
These research papers, 
several generations ahead of our time,

10:52.040 --> 10:55.170
suggested the possibility 
of unseen properties.

10:55.620 --> 10:58.490
Due to the fact that we've 
been proceeding with caution,

10:58.490 --> 11:00.760
we have yet to report this 
to even the royal family!

11:00.760 --> 11:02.340
And yet you...

11:02.640 --> 11:05.400
Your insight is simply astonishing!

11:05.810 --> 11:08.810
I've never dreamed of such talent!

11:10.120 --> 11:12.110
How about it, Haruto Zenfis?!

11:12.110 --> 11:15.560
Leave that research lab studying 
utterly useless ancient magic

11:15.560 --> 11:17.600
and come work under me!

11:17.600 --> 11:20.380
Th-That'll be a no from me.

11:20.380 --> 11:21.790
Professor Belkam.

11:21.790 --> 11:25.450
Recruitment during lessons 
is simply unbecoming of you.

11:25.680 --> 11:27.710
Then you should join us, as well!

11:27.710 --> 11:29.630
I already said I wouldn't.

11:29.630 --> 11:31.460
Haruto Zenfis.

11:31.460 --> 11:35.320
You wouldn't happen to actually 
be Weße Eule, would you?!

11:36.420 --> 11:37.830
No way!

11:37.830 --> 11:38.920
Sparkle!

11:38.920 --> 11:41.010
<i>Weiße Eule, huh?</i>

11:38.920 --> 11:45.550
<b>Weiße Eule</b>

11:38.920 --> 11:45.550
<b>"White Owl"</b>

11:41.010 --> 11:43.650
<i>Who could be behind that cool-sounding name?</i>

11:43.650 --> 11:45.550
<i>I'd also love to know.</i>

11:46.120 --> 11:49.150
You're really an amazing guy, you know that?

11:49.150 --> 11:51.060
That's Haruto for you!

11:56.570 --> 11:57.940
<b>Am I Actually the Strongest?</b>

11:59.790 --> 12:00.910
I see.

12:01.220 --> 12:04.380
It looks like you finally 
understand the passion I hold.

12:07.920 --> 12:12.530
Now the research lab can continue 
to operate until they graduate!

12:12.530 --> 12:13.100
<i>What?!</i>

12:13.100 --> 12:14.700
That was the reason?!

12:14.700 --> 12:17.860
With that settled, we should 
hold a welcome party!

12:17.860 --> 12:20.760
Polkos, you're in charge of the food!

12:20.760 --> 12:21.420
Right away!

12:21.420 --> 12:24.480
You two just relax and wait right there!

12:28.850 --> 12:31.480
<i>Sheesh, why me?</i>

12:31.480 --> 12:33.750
<i>It was supposed to be 
my original self today!</i>

12:36.360 --> 12:38.120
A lot happened, so I'm tired.

12:38.120 --> 12:38.970
I'm begging you.

12:40.200 --> 12:42.830
<i>I mean, I handed in my application form.</i>

12:43.060 --> 12:44.870
<i>I can leave, right?</i>

12:46.460 --> 12:47.380
Oh?

12:47.380 --> 12:49.760
Looks like something happened to Polkos.

12:49.760 --> 12:51.520
Let's all go check it out!

12:55.490 --> 12:58.210
<i>A-A murder scene?!</i>

12:58.530 --> 13:00.620
<i>Wait, no, it's Schneidel!</i>

13:00.620 --> 13:02.750
Ah, I forgot about him.

13:02.750 --> 13:05.050
That's right, he was here.

13:05.050 --> 13:06.340
She<i> did this?!</i>

13:06.820 --> 13:09.440
He suddenly showed up at my door yesterday.

13:09.440 --> 13:11.230
He'd been afflicted with a strange spell,

13:11.230 --> 13:13.440
so he asked me to look into it.

13:13.440 --> 13:16.010
It was magic that he had never come across,

13:16.010 --> 13:18.180
so he suspected it might be ancient magic.

13:18.180 --> 13:20.300
And so, after all manners of investigation,

13:20.300 --> 13:22.690
by dawn, a state of complete 
exhaustion was reached.

13:22.690 --> 13:24.630
By him, of course.

13:24.630 --> 13:27.790
<i>What did she do to reduce him to this?!</i>

13:27.790 --> 13:29.400
But this is our chance.

13:29.400 --> 13:34.320
Since he's here, let's use him to 
research ancient magic together!

13:34.320 --> 13:35.160
<i>That's awful!</i>

13:35.560 --> 13:36.790
Iris.

13:36.790 --> 13:39.410
Why don't you try touching 
his right shoulder?

13:39.790 --> 13:40.630
Yes...

13:45.360 --> 13:48.120
Something solid is attached to him?

13:48.120 --> 13:50.470
Clear, colorless cylinders?

13:50.810 --> 13:51.810
That's right.

13:51.810 --> 13:54.770
And when magic is used to 
heal the wound, for example,

13:54.770 --> 13:57.140
the two cylinders attract each other,

13:57.140 --> 14:00.200
squeezing his shoulder tightly like so.

14:00.510 --> 14:03.450
But this is the really interesting part.

14:03.450 --> 14:05.450
When you do this...

14:06.350 --> 14:07.920
Look! It passes right through.

14:08.360 --> 14:12.090
It looks like anything inanimate 
goes right through it.

14:12.090 --> 14:14.090
What do you think this is?

14:15.920 --> 14:18.450
Wait, is it non-elemental magic?

14:18.450 --> 14:19.560
Impressive!

14:19.560 --> 14:22.130
No wonder you got top marks 
on the written exam!

14:22.130 --> 14:25.920
In other words, this is a barrier 
made using non-elemental magic.

14:25.920 --> 14:26.720
Huh?

14:27.130 --> 14:31.150
<i>This teacher figured out the 
truth behind the barrier?</i>

14:31.150 --> 14:34.870
<i>But that doesn't mean that she's seen 
through my original self's identity.</i>

14:34.870 --> 14:36.420
Okay, Haruto.

14:36.420 --> 14:40.670
Can you tell me the biggest difference 
between modern and ancient magic?

14:41.940 --> 14:43.490
Uh...

14:43.490 --> 14:46.230
The fact that it's really old magic?

14:46.690 --> 14:47.570
Siiiiigh

14:47.700 --> 14:48.450
Tsk!

14:47.700 --> 14:48.900
<b>That annoyed me,
but hold it in...</b>

14:49.270 --> 14:50.660
Take it away, Iris.

14:50.860 --> 14:59.120
<b>Void</b>

14:50.980 --> 14:55.000
Ancient magic is non-elemental magic, 
not bound to any one element.

14:55.000 --> 14:59.110
As an ancient lost magic, 
it contains many mysteries.

14:59.110 --> 15:00.220
Indeed.

15:00.220 --> 15:05.790
And records say that it can be maintained 
without supplying any mana.

15:06.140 --> 15:10.670
If this were modern magic, it wouldn't last 
half a day before you'd run out of mana.

15:10.670 --> 15:14.640
But it's been one and a half days 
since it was placed on him.

15:14.640 --> 15:15.870
That can't be!

15:15.870 --> 15:19.520
Are you saying that there's someone in 
modern times who can use ancient magic?!

15:19.520 --> 15:22.060
Well, it's little more than a theory.

15:22.440 --> 15:27.390
As you know, it's magic from the distant past, 
wielded by those from the mythical era.

15:27.390 --> 15:32.110
You'd probably have to be above 
level 80, at least, to use it.

15:32.590 --> 15:38.070
Which begs the question, 
who could have possibly cast this spell?

15:38.370 --> 15:39.650
It's not me.

15:39.650 --> 15:42.530
I can't use such advanced magic.

15:44.710 --> 15:45.880
Hmm...

15:45.880 --> 15:48.350
It doesn't seem like you're 
feigning ignorance.

15:48.750 --> 15:53.340
Though he mentioned that you 
happened to be there at the time.

15:53.640 --> 15:56.720
I don't know who did it, either.

15:56.720 --> 15:57.890
I see.

15:57.890 --> 16:01.500
I guess we'll need to ask the culprit.

16:03.020 --> 16:06.870
Last night, he refused 
to tell me who did it.

16:06.870 --> 16:09.820
It's about time he finally snapped!

16:11.930 --> 16:14.300
What are <i>you</i> doing here?!

16:14.300 --> 16:16.500
Oh, did you finally notice?

16:16.500 --> 16:18.010
How dare you!

16:18.010 --> 16:20.340
You know that I'm the Hafen family heir...

16:20.340 --> 16:23.000
We're all fully aware of that!

16:23.000 --> 16:24.310
Listen to me.

16:24.310 --> 16:26.210
Let me get right to the point.

16:26.210 --> 16:28.590
I can't remove this hex of yours.

16:29.140 --> 16:32.840
Which means the only one who 
can is the one who cast it.

16:32.840 --> 16:35.460
How about you spill the beans already?

16:37.980 --> 16:39.960
I don't know who it was.

16:39.960 --> 16:43.890
It was a man with a strange voice, 
clad entirely in black.

16:43.890 --> 16:48.350
So you found it humiliating to be 
done in by a mysterious villain?

16:48.850 --> 16:49.660
No...

16:49.660 --> 16:53.680
Perhaps your life would be in 
danger if you revealed that fact.

16:54.270 --> 16:55.200
I see.

16:55.200 --> 16:58.830
Well, from the scant information we have,

16:58.830 --> 17:00.910
there's one person I can 
think of who fits the bill.

17:01.160 --> 17:02.110
What?

17:02.920 --> 17:04.260
Haruto.

17:04.260 --> 17:06.830
I hear that in the border province,

17:06.830 --> 17:10.470
there's a hero of justice who started 
showing up several years ago.

17:10.820 --> 17:14.000
His description matches the 
one Schneidel just gave.

17:14.000 --> 17:15.680
Do you know who he is?

17:15.990 --> 17:17.990
No, I don't.

17:18.360 --> 17:22.380
That said, he only used to operate 
within the border province,

17:22.380 --> 17:26.260
and now he's appeared in the royal 
capital, at the same time Haruto did.

17:26.530 --> 17:30.940
He must have... had some 
sort of business here.

17:30.940 --> 17:32.310
Interesting.

17:32.570 --> 17:38.780
Should I start by asking why you were 
recommended by the king himself?

17:39.530 --> 17:42.980
You can ask me that, but I don't the reason.

17:44.000 --> 17:47.110
What is it, exactly, that you're hiding?!

17:47.110 --> 17:51.980
Could it be that you have knowledge 
of ancient magic that I don't?!

17:52.710 --> 17:56.160
Why don't you just tell 
us everything right now?!

17:56.160 --> 17:59.690
Actually, are <i>you</i> the 
one dressed in all black?

17:56.180 --> 18:02.060
<b>Menacing</b>

17:59.690 --> 18:02.070
If so, I'd love to hear about it!

18:02.070 --> 18:04.270
Why don't we spend some time,

18:04.270 --> 18:06.690
and you can tell me <i>all</i> about it!

18:06.690 --> 18:09.770
<i>Why am </i>I<i> always the one who 
has to deal with this?!</i>

18:09.770 --> 18:10.490
<i>I've had enough!</i>

18:10.490 --> 18:12.830
<i>Save me, original self!</i>

18:13.400 --> 18:14.920
I see you're talking about me.

18:16.170 --> 18:19.570
Shiva, the embodiment of 
justice, has arrived!

18:20.990 --> 18:23.610
<i>The fact that he showed up at this moment...</i>

18:24.020 --> 18:26.860
<i>You were watching us all along, you jerk!</i>

18:27.260 --> 18:29.160
You, the small one in glasses.

18:29.160 --> 18:31.690
I am completely unaffiliated with that boy.

18:31.690 --> 18:35.340
I came here to enact justice upon the 
evildoers who bring chaos to the capital.

18:35.340 --> 18:36.370
Oh!

18:36.370 --> 18:38.680
So <i>you're</i> the famous Shiva!

18:38.680 --> 18:41.630
Skinny, but with some good 
muscle on that frame.

18:41.630 --> 18:43.880
That smooth helm of yours 
is fashionable, too!

18:43.880 --> 18:45.300
<i>Were you even listening?</i>

18:45.300 --> 18:47.290
Evildoers, you say...

18:47.290 --> 18:52.230
So you were aware that this rich heir 
is a member of a suspicious group?

18:53.270 --> 18:54.380
<i>Huh?</i>

18:53.270 --> 18:59.910
Villain

18:54.380 --> 18:58.000
<i>The evil syndicate really existed?</i>

18:58.000 --> 18:59.890
<i>Okay, let's go along with that.</i>

19:00.320 --> 19:01.450
That's right.

19:01.450 --> 19:03.240
I know all about that.

19:03.240 --> 19:05.890
But leaving that aside, Schneidel.

19:06.920 --> 19:10.190
If you heed my warning 
and call off the duel,

19:10.190 --> 19:12.290
I'll free you of your shackles 
by tomorrow morning.

19:12.550 --> 19:14.880
Y-You bastard...

19:15.250 --> 19:16.540
Any objections?

19:21.910 --> 19:23.210
Very well.

19:23.610 --> 19:26.780
With that, I shall take my leave...

19:26.780 --> 19:28.190
At least, I'd like to, but...

19:29.520 --> 19:31.180
What is the meaning of this?

19:32.760 --> 19:34.650
You let your guard down.

19:36.570 --> 19:39.980
You really didn't notice my binding magic?!

19:40.290 --> 19:42.740
<i>Mana Calculator: Revised.</i>

19:43.870 --> 19:49.910
Tearietta Luseiannel
[33] / [36]

[Earth] 100
[Darkness] 71
[Fire] 44
[Wind] 41
[Water] 28

19:45.240 --> 19:46.470
<i>I see.</i>

19:46.470 --> 19:49.920
<i>A blend of earth and dark elements?</i>

19:50.250 --> 19:53.040
<b>Earth / Darkness</b>

19:50.250 --> 19:53.050
<i>That's why it's stronger than earth alone.</i>

19:53.460 --> 19:57.590
Not even you can undo that spell so easily.

19:57.810 --> 20:03.550
And I can't have you leaving before you've 
answered the 271 questions I have for you!

20:06.760 --> 20:07.530
Huh?

20:07.530 --> 20:10.050
How did you neutralize it?!

20:10.050 --> 20:13.000
And why am I completely immobilized?!

20:13.000 --> 20:15.070
It's payback for binding me just now.

20:15.070 --> 20:17.210
Amazing. Polkos!

20:17.210 --> 20:19.520
This is complete domain fixation here!

20:19.520 --> 20:21.230
Spare us the analysis!

20:21.230 --> 20:22.700
Just apologize already!

20:22.700 --> 20:27.540
I'd love to, but the number of 
questions has gone up to 824!

20:27.540 --> 20:28.460
I'm so curious!

20:28.460 --> 20:30.080
Will you please answer them?

20:30.080 --> 20:32.450
Seriously, you're being rude!

20:32.450 --> 20:33.790
I see.

20:33.790 --> 20:35.590
You want me to offer something of value.

20:35.590 --> 20:37.510
She's not listening at all!

20:37.510 --> 20:40.540
I know! How about my chastity?!

20:40.540 --> 20:42.960
Your satisfaction is guaranteed!

20:44.930 --> 20:46.610
For crying out loud!

20:46.610 --> 20:47.880
You big dummy!

20:47.880 --> 20:49.710
What now?!

20:50.610 --> 20:52.180
I need to pee.

20:54.370 --> 20:56.650
Stop looking into me.

20:56.650 --> 20:57.980
You're gonna say that <i>now</i>?!

20:57.980 --> 21:00.640
You're quite the skilled negotiator.

21:00.640 --> 21:01.960
I'm impressed!

21:01.960 --> 21:04.920
So can you please undo this right away?

21:05.590 --> 21:06.900
Your answer?

21:06.900 --> 21:08.760
Oh, yeah, I'll stop!

21:08.760 --> 21:12.030
I don't want to pee myself 
in front of my students!

21:14.500 --> 21:17.310
I'll stop! I'm sorry!

21:17.310 --> 21:19.000
The dam's about to burst!

21:19.530 --> 21:21.570
I see. It's a promise.

21:22.950 --> 21:24.350
I bid you farewell.

21:28.190 --> 21:29.130
Professor!

21:29.130 --> 21:31.630
I-I can move again, Polkos!

21:31.630 --> 21:32.830
The restroom! Hurry!

21:32.830 --> 21:35.120
Th-That's right!

21:35.120 --> 21:38.490
Bathroom!

23:08.950 --> 23:23.960
m 0 0 l 110 0 l 102 22 l 0 22

23:08.950 --> 23:23.960
Episode Preview

23:09.680 --> 23:11.260
Charlotte here!

23:11.260 --> 23:13.530
Haruto, good job going to school!

23:13.530 --> 23:15.240
I'm sure you must be very tired!

23:15.240 --> 23:17.890
I was praying for your safety from afar!

23:17.890 --> 23:19.750
Next episode: "Not a Bad Night".

23:18.160 --> 23:18.410
<b>Lovely</b>

23:18.500 --> 23:23.950
<b>Not a Bad Night</b>

23:19.750 --> 23:20.380
Huh?

23:20.380 --> 23:21.770
Next week is the finale?

23:21.770 --> 23:22.900
Really?
